      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Angles and Magnitudes",
      "problem": "Suppose $|\\,a\\,|=14$ and the angle between vectors $a$ and $b$ is $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.$ Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =14\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =14\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
