      "reasoning": "All 16 answers agree with their own captured worked solutions. q-112964: reducing and deduplicating the rational-root candidates gives 10 positive magnitudes and their negatives, totaling 20. q-288814: Vieta's product is -14/7=-2. q-3762: equal polynomial degrees give the leading-coefficient ratio -2/6=-1/3. q-48713: for sufficiently large positive x, |7x-4|=7x-4, giving 7/2. q-68042: the expression behaves like 3x and tends to positive infinity. q-35763: the denominator has greater degree, giving horizontal asymptote y=0. q-101321 and q-35834: the functions behave like (4/3)x^3 and -x^2, respectively, so neither has a horizontal asymptote at either end. q-101522: the scalar projection is 14 cos(2π/3)=-7. q-18374: the projection is (3-√3)/√12=(√3-1)/2. q-237020: zero projection requires 6+3x=0, giving x=-2. q-237018: zero projection requires -32-4x=0, giving x=-8. q-70275: every real square is nonnegative, so there are no solutions. q-83840: the distinct positive rational-root candidates are 1/2, 1, 2, 7/2, 7, and 14, totaling 12 with negatives. q-112875: -3 is the only listed choice excluded by the rational roots theorem; inclusion among potential roots does not establish an actual root. q-288815: Vieta's product is -27/9=-3.",
